1. I think the moonlight scene was easiest to create, since changing the lighting was simple and moving the light upwards was also very easy.
2. The campfire looked most realistic to me, I like how it turned out. I think the shadows are very strong and the lighting really reflects what it's like to have minimal light at night.
3. Changing ambient lighting made the shadows more apparent if lower and less if higher.
4. Certain faces of the shapes became darker/brighter if they were facing the light.
5. The orange lighting in the sunset/campfire felt strongest and most apparent to me.
6. It helps with realism and immersion if the lighting replicates real life light and shadows. 
7. Low ambient lighting and somewhat similar to the moonlight scene. It helps obscure the full shape of certain objects and keeps things dark, making it scarier. 
